{"title":"2004 OIM Problems/Problem 5","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_OIM_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Given a scalene triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" />, Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/a/94afe0a61d5d8031fdb59c1c27eb768234751ed3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A&#39;, B&#39;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"44\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/7/9b798193cb94562989018728e1151587c618655b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C&#39;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"16\" /> the points of intersection of the interior bisectors of angles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/f/bef747a48a2a8d43c4841e12c89f2de2502a672e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A, B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"35\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> with the opposite sides, respectively.  Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/e/81ecc8352ed830fa97109845526d1ff032b5e583.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A&#39;&#39;$\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> be the intersection of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> with the perpendicular bisector of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/9/d59f5d75cc27d504ede022aab803742e799709f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AA&#39;$\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />; <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/0/1b022eeb8c4f5a764deebc4015180e6be55304b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B&#39;&#39;$\" width=\"22\" height=\"14\" /> be the intersection of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> with the perpendicular bisector of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/a/c2ae0e30605dc87c83aecb3f588afa7129bee6aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BB&#39;$\" width=\"33\" height=\"14\" />; and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/0/b308fa72944d6d8bc35bbe5386d00bc511a04efb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C&#39;&#39;$\" width=\"22\" height=\"14\" /> be the intersection of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> with the perpendicular bisector of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/b/44b7058f8a28ca225136b284b337138a54e39e8c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CC&#39;$\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" />.  Prove that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/e/81ecc8352ed830fa97109845526d1ff032b5e583.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A&#39;&#39;$\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/0/1b022eeb8c4f5a764deebc4015180e6be55304b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B&#39;&#39;$\" width=\"22\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/0/b308fa72944d6d8bc35bbe5386d00bc511a04efb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C&#39;&#39;$\" width=\"22\" height=\"14\" /> are collinear.\n</p><p>~translated into English by Tomas Diaz. ~orders@tomasdiaz.com\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_OIM_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><i>This problem needs a solution. If you have a solution for it, please help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2004_OIM_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit\">adding it</a></span>.</i> \n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_OIM_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=OIM_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"OIM Problems and Solutions\">OIM Problems and Solutions</a>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017004010\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.012 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.015 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 101/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 423/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 2777/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    5.329      1 Template:Solution\n100.00%    5.329      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:26334:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017004010 and revision id 207483. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}